<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Divine kingship</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Divine kingship is the idea that a ruler is a god or possesses divine status. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naram-sin">Naram-Sin</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> claimed divinity, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer Empire</a> built its state around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devaraja">devaraja</a> cult, and rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a> held sacred status. The concept also appears, by contrast or in other forms, in the profiles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>.</p></div>
